  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#47584\", \"PowerToys#45592\", \"PowerToys#48538\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before. The Command Palette dock hides when Win+D, the Show Desktop button or the trackpad gesture is used. It has been tracked since the dock was first released. #47584 is the main tracking issue, and #48538 was closed as a duplicate of it. In #45592 a maintainer said the code to keep the dock visible (the ShowDesktop helper in DockWindow.xaml.cs) works most of the time but not reliably. No fix or workaround is confirmed in those tickets. Please subscribe to #47584 and add your PowerToys and Windows versions and any taskbar tools you run, such as TranslucentTB. One reporter in #48538 saw the dock stay visible while certain windows were open, such as file Properties. In #48233 the behavior stopped on its own for one user.\"}",
